    "body": "PSG and France international winger Désiré Doué (21) has torn his right anterior cruciate ligament, according to L’Equipe . Doué’s right knee gave way on itself during today’s 3 -2 away win against OGC Nice. The Rennes Academy graduate may be out for the remainder of the Ligue 1 season. It is a considerable injury blow for PSG, only a month after Khvicha Kvaratskhelia had sustained a similar injury. PSG’s worst fears are set to be confirmed on Sunday with Doué poised to undergo an MRI, but the outlet reports that both PSG’s medical staff and Doué are adamant that the latter has sustained a serious knee injury. PSG head coach Luis Enrique already told reporters that Doué’s injury was severe . PSG may be forced to dip into the transfer market this winter to bolster Luis Enrique’s options upfront as both Doué and Kvaratskhelia will be sidelined for several months, and that Mika Godts hasn’t really impressed since his summer move from AFC Ajax. PSG will host AS Roma for Matchday 5 of the UEFA Champions League next week. GFFN | Bastien Cheval",
