    "title_key": "rayasettohavescanoninjuryhowmuchwouldarsenalmisshim",
    "body": "Image source, Getty Images Image caption, David Raya has made 163 appearances since joining Arsenal in 2023 Arsenal reporter at St James' Park Published 3 hours ago Injuries are never good news, but Arsenal 's latest one to first-choice goalkeeper David Raya has come in the worst possible position. The 31-year-old was forced to leave the pitch 70 minutes into Saturday's 2-2 draw with Newcastle , appearing to hurt his shoulder in an innocuous challenge with Magpies forward William Osula. The Gunners arguably have the best depth in the league with at least two quality options in all outfield positions after a period of squad strengthening. In goal, however, cover appears much thinner. Raya was a key component in Arsenal 's Premier League title-winning campaign last season, was named in the Fifpro Men's World 11 and was unlucky to not win the Yashin Trophy, awarded to the world's best goalkeeper, which went to Spain team-mate Unai Simon. Behind him, Kepa Arrizabalaga still holds the record as the most expensive goalkeeper in football history following his £72m move from Athletic Bilbao to Chelsea in August 2018, but is far behind Raya in terms of quality. Raya's passing range and ability on the ball are key to how Arsenal build their attacks, and his presence is a big reason why they have the best defence in the league. They have conceded just seven Premier League goals this season, with only Brighton able to match that tally - having played a game fewer. Arsenal also brought in",
